00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:17.310
I am sending you on a new quest to solve a
427-year-old mystery, starring Ivan the Terrible.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:23.430
He's looking at me, isn't he? Uwuughhh! You're
so scary looking. Why are you looking at me?

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.039
Okay Hank, first off when it comes to Kings
and Tsars, 'Great' does not mean better than

00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:30.949
good, and 'Terrible' does not mean worse than
bad, although that's a common mistake. 'Great'

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:33.719
and 'Terrible' in their classical meanings
are actually quite similar, they both have

00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:36.510
connotations of power and might and authority.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.699
Okay Hank, picture this - I know I need to
button the button - you're three years old

00:00:39.699 --> 00:00:45.030
and your dad dies of a leg boil. You wanna
know why it's better to be middle class in

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:50.989
the 21st century, than it is to be incredibly
rich in the 15th century? Very rarely do people

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:54.212
currently die of leg boils. Right so you're
three years old and your dad dies, which means

00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:58.429
that technically you're now the King of Russia,
which is a terrible gig because like, you're

00:00:58.429 --> 00:01:02.549
mostly potty trained, but you're not totally
ready to run a country.

00:01:02.549 --> 00:01:07.540
So that means you need a regent. Fortunately,
your mom is available to be your regent. Unfortunately,

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.659
when you're eight, the nobility kills her.

00:01:09.659 --> 00:01:13.510
So you're eight, you've got all these nobility,
these boyers, running around the palace fighting

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:17.829
with each other over who should rule the show,
and you hate them. Because they killed your

00:01:17.829 --> 00:01:21.049
mom, and they also make you nervous because
they might kill you.

00:01:21.049 --> 00:01:24.340
But when you turn 16 and you take over the
throne you decide "Y'know I'm not going to

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.460
focus all my energy on negativity, on getting
rid of these boyers. I'm gonna make the world

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.460
better"

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:33.730
You modernize the legal code, you open up
trade with Europe, you annex a bunch of land

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:38.179
and make Russia look more like... Russia,
and you marry this beautiful girl named Anastasia.

00:01:38.179 --> 00:01:41.840
Hank, here is a lesson from history: Never
be Russian and named Anastasia.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.820
Yeah so then in 1560, your wife dies and you
think the boyers did it, and you're like "They

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:51.429
killed my mom, they made me very anxious when
I was a child, and now, I think they killed

00:01:51.429 --> 00:01:56.090
my wife". So then you start to be more traditionally
terrible. You start a really ill-advised war,

00:01:56.090 --> 00:02:00.749
you have this quasi-police force that goes
around massacring boyers and also anyone else

00:02:00.749 --> 00:02:05.289
they come across, and then you beat your pregnant
daughter-in-law until she has a miscarriage,

00:02:05.289 --> 00:02:09.979
and then your son Ivan-should've-been-the-fifth
comes up to you and he's like "Dad, I wish

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:13.940
you hadn't done that" and you kill him. In
your defense, you didn't mean to kill him,

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:17.080
you meant to, y'know, hit him. But he died.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:20.830
But Hank, in your role as Ivan the Terrible,
that is not even the worst thing you ever

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:28.400
did. The worst was this - 427 years ago you
died! In the middle of a chess game! Without

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.560
telling anyone where your incredibly fancy
library is!

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.610
Sorry, I get very upset when people screw
around with libraries.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.630
Your grandfather, Ivan the Third, married
a Byzantine lady. By Byzantine, I don't mean

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:44.660
like, complicated, I mean like of Byzantium.
As her dowry, she brought with her a beautiful

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:50.590
library full of illuminated manuscripts encrusted
in jewels so valuable that the king of Russia

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.720
was like "Man, we have got to hide this".

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:58.160
So they built an underground library somewhere
underneath Moscow - there are like thousands

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.500
of miles of tunnels underneath Moscow because
it's the perfect sand for tunneling, or something.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.940
And that would have worked fine except Ivan
the Terrible was so obsessed with killing

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.590
boyers and expanding Russia and becoming the
first real Tsar that he completely forgot

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:14.420
about the library and died without telling
anyone where it was.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.570
In short Hank, if the legends are true, there
are right now underneath Moscow billions of

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:23.590
dollars worth of books. And so for the last
427 years, people have been searching for

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:28.200
it. Nerdfighters, that is my task for you!
I have created a thread in Your Pants - link

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:33.060
in the doobly doo - where together, we can
search out information so that we might uncover

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.400
